{"kind":"artifact","text":"Chess item 2, round 2: internal/app selects the interpreter once, when a workspace opens, and reports kernel verification ahead of any refusal to interpret. A replacement binding recorded after an open is read by the next open, so no operation changes meaning because of activity that followed the open; the lazy selection state is gone; a repository whose log cannot be read does not open; an unopened workspace refuses rather than folding with an interpreter it never selected. Snapshot and AcceptSubmission both audit before they report a refusal, so an unverifiable chain is reported as a sequencer signature failure rather than as a missing interpreter. internal/kernel is byte-identical to main. go build, go vet and go test ./... -count=1 all green at this head.","body":{"commit":"3248befa30a54338b9ce6d29a92adc36637733f3","path":"internal/app"}}